Main Purpose of the Job
We have an exciting position for an Intern or full status Rental Agent to take on the role of growing a long-term letting residential rental portfolio in the Atlantic Seaboard area (Cape Town). It is a great opportunity to join a dynamic rentals office. The area is a buoyant market consisting of a mix of foreign and local landlords and tenants. It is a great opportunity for a passionate, energetic, full status agent to grow and expand the portfolio consisting of long-term letting residential properties.
Key Responsibilities
Managing the maintenance of rental properties to ensure that they are well maintained;
Showing vacant units to prospective tenants, answering their questions about the property and area, and processing lease applications;
Conducting background checks on prospective tenants to ensure that they have suitable financial backgrounds, employment histories, and criminal records;
Reviewing applications and other documentation to determine if applicants meet criteria specified by landlords;
Negotiating lease terms with tenants on behalf of landlords;
Preparing lease agreements for signature by both parties, including landlords and tenants;
Maintaining rental property inventories by conducting inspections of each unit on a regular basis;
Doing and recording comprehensive ingoing and outgoing property inspections when lease commence / terminate;
Dealing with and resolving landlord / tenant queries and disputes;
Managing monthly rental payments and follow up on arrear rental payments;
Growing the existing portfolio.
Key Competencies
A high level of integrity, credibility and ethics are all non-negotiable;
Self-motivated, energetic and passionate about Rentals;
Excellent communicator;
The ability to cope with pressure and setbacks is an important skill in our industry;
Willingness to be available outside of normal working hours.
Education & Experience
Grade 12/ Matric;
The candidate must have his or her own reliable transport and be willing to work flexible hours;
Your own laptop and access to reliable wifi is essential.
Knowledge & Skills Required
Knowledge of the Atlantic Seaboard and the surrounding areas rental market would be beneficial but not compulsory;
Superior negotiation skills;
Strong planning and organisation skills with an eye for detail.
Deadline:6th March,2026

